      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im doing a lit review for my phd and im stuck on citations. if a paper has like 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th vs chicago style? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For APA 7th edition, when citing a source with five authors in-text, you list the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" from the very first citation. In Chicago style (Notes and Bibliography), you use a footnote that typically includes the first author's last name and the page number on subsequent citations if you are using short forms. Be sure to check your specific departmental guidelines, as methods can vary slightly.",
