      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so for chicago, is it just the name and page number for the short form? i dont want to mess up the footnote format if i'm citing it multiple times in a row. also is there a specific way to handle it if the first author is the same as a previous citation?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, for short-form Chicago footnotes, it is generally the author's last name and a shortened title followed by the page number. If the first author is the same as a previous citation, you can use a shortened form that includes the author and a specific reference to the previous full note, often using \"Ibid.\" if it's the very same source immediately before. This consistent referencing helps maintain clarity throughout your footnotes.",
